    "created_at": "2024-11-25T17:29:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-11-25T17:29:14Z",
    "body": "\"In parallel\" has a common meaning in English, which does not match the intended meaning here.\r\n\r\n\"Run the following steps in parallel\" would *usually* mean, \"run each of these steps in parallel with the others\", not \"run these steps as a sequence, in parallel with any other actions, sequences, functions, etc.\"\r\n\r\nThe whole `Parallelism` section needs some revision, such that `run this list of steps in parallel` (which implies `with each other`) is no longer used to mean `run these actions in series, in parallel with actions not in this list`.\r\n\r\nI discovered this issue while trying to address a confusing section of [FedCM](https://github.com/w3c-fedid/FedCM/pull/678#discussion_r1834999800).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
